# ============================================================================
# Environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored.
# NAMES ONLY IN THIS FILE — never commit a real key.
#
# Email ADDRESSES are not here. They are public, non-secret application
# configuration and live in lib/email.ts (public aliases) and
# lib/email.server.ts (the private inbox and From identities). Putting a
# non-secret address behind an env var adds a deployment step that can be
# missed silently — producing a contact form that appears to work and
# delivers nowhere.
# ============================================================================

# Resend API key — https://resend.com/api-keys
# The only secret this application needs.
#
# NAME IS LOWERCASE AND THAT IS DELIBERATE: it matches the variable already
# provisioned in Vercel. process.env is case-sensitive on Linux, so
# RESEND_API_KEY would read as undefined in production.
#
# Required for the contact form to send. Without it the form returns a generic
# error to the visitor and logs the missing-config detail server-side; it never
# breaks the build.
#
# Before launch, verify markfasel.dev in Resend (SPF + DKIM). Mail sends from
# notifications@markfasel.dev and hello@markfasel.dev — both must be on a
# verified domain or delivery lands in spam.
resend_api=
